<p>
When I'm working with a tutor to improve my French, I sometimes need
to push myself to provide more details when I'm sharing and ask more
follow-up questions in response to what they're saying, instead of
falling back to « D'accord » and « C'est cool. » Visualizing the
timeline in real-time lets me see if the turn-taking looks good. I
might even need to take a more active role in controlling the
conversation if I happen to be meeting a tutor who tends to go on
monologues.
</p>

<p>
When I'm talking out loud on my own for practice, this might also
nudge me to reduce the pauses and enrich my vocabulary by practising
saying things often enough that they become more automatic.
</p>
